From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:34:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 412/488] Sink detector: the greedy shard candidates and the
 merge as TileLang kernels

A greedy step's alternates ran torch.topk over each rank's vocabulary
shard (20 kernels at DS4.1's shard width), a cat, and the merge's
masked_fill, stable sort and gathers. One kernel a request now picks the
shard's k best columns and writes the packed row the ranks gather; one
kernel a request merges them (and the sampled path's candidates). The
merge equals torch's bit for bit. The shard candidates order equal values
by column, the order the full-logits path and the merge already assume;
torch.topk left their order undefined, so only an exact tie at a sink
event can choose differently.
